1
00:00:01,303 --> 00:00:04,878
Somewhere right now, a security operator is watching forty

2
00:00:04,898 --> 00:00:06,050
camera feeds.

3
00:00:06,239 --> 00:00:08,306
Their attention can be on only one.

4
00:00:08,481 --> 00:00:10,471
And in the few seconds they look away,

5
00:00:10,491 --> 00:00:13,499
a weapon appears, smoke begins to rise,

6
00:00:13,648 --> 00:00:16,140
or a person of interest slips out of view.

7
00:00:17,623 --> 00:00:19,485
This is VigiLense:

8
00:00:19,505 --> 00:00:23,338
an AI surveillance and incident response system that watches

9
00:00:23,358 --> 00:00:26,160
every feed, understands what it sees,

10
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:28,544
and brings the most critical moment straight to the

11
00:00:28,564 --> 00:00:29,433
operator.

12
00:00:30,923 --> 00:00:35,168
Conventional CCTV depends almost entirely on human attention.

13
00:00:35,343 --> 00:00:38,442
In universities, shopping malls, hospitals,

14
00:00:38,462 --> 00:00:41,122
airports, banks and railway stations,

15
00:00:41,155 --> 00:00:44,317
operators must observe many screens at once.

16
00:00:44,493 --> 00:00:47,269
The result is fatigue, missed incidents,

17
00:00:47,289 --> 00:00:50,567
delayed response, and poor situational awareness.

18
00:00:52,086 --> 00:00:53,534
These systems are passive.

19
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:56,757
They record and display, but they cannot recognise a

20
00:00:56,777 --> 00:00:58,883
weapon, fire or smoke.

21
00:00:59,058 --> 00:01:01,692
A critical event can unfold on a feed that

22
00:01:01,712 --> 00:01:03,277
is not on the main screen.

23
00:01:03,452 --> 00:01:05,532
And when a person moves from one camera to

24
00:01:05,552 --> 00:01:09,707
another, tracking ends, especially when their face is hidden,

25
00:01:09,754 --> 00:01:11,460
covered, or turned away.

26
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:15,935
VigiLense answers this with clear objectives.

27
00:01:16,123 --> 00:01:20,342
Build a real-time prototype with Ultralytics YOLO26,

28
00:01:20,389 --> 00:01:22,379
OpenCV and Python.

29
00:01:22,554 --> 00:01:24,827
Monitor at least three camera feeds.

30
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:28,345
Detect persons, weapons, fire and smoke.

31
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,664
Track people within each camera,

32
00:01:30,711 --> 00:01:33,333
and follow a selected person across cameras with a

33
00:01:33,353 --> 00:01:34,428
global ID.

34
00:01:34,603 --> 00:01:37,998
Then prioritise events, switch the most important feed to

35
00:01:38,018 --> 00:01:40,600
the dashboard, notify the operator,

36
00:01:40,646 --> 00:01:42,919
and log every incident with evidence.

37
00:01:44,436 --> 00:01:45,575
Here is how it works.

38
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:48,488
Each camera source, whether CCTV,

39
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:52,495
IP, RTSP, webcam or recorded video,

40
00:01:52,645 --> 00:01:55,343
is registered with an ID and a location.

41
00:01:55,518 --> 00:01:59,364
OpenCV captures each stream, extracts frames,

42
00:01:59,384 --> 00:02:03,590
and resizes, normalises and enhances them for analysis.

43
00:02:05,093 --> 00:02:07,947
YOLO26 is the main detection model.

44
00:02:08,173 --> 00:02:10,808
For every frame it returns object classes,

45
00:02:10,828 --> 00:02:13,205
bounding boxes and confidence scores,

46
00:02:13,225 --> 00:02:16,903
for persons, weapon-like objects, fire and smoke.

47
00:02:17,091 --> 00:02:19,622
Pretrained models are fine-tuned on public,

48
00:02:19,668 --> 00:02:21,916
authorised and controlled datasets.

49
00:02:23,403 --> 00:02:27,610
Next, ByteTrack or BoT-SORT gives every person a local

50
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:30,212
tracking ID inside each camera,

51
00:02:30,259 --> 00:02:33,009
keeping identities stable from frame to frame,

52
00:02:33,184 --> 00:02:34,246
even in a crowd.

53
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:38,274
When an operator marks a person of interest,

54
00:02:38,295 --> 00:02:40,735
VigiLense extracts their appearance:

55
00:02:40,769 --> 00:02:44,035
clothing, body shape, helmet, bag,

56
00:02:44,068 --> 00:02:45,478
and other accessories.

57
00:02:45,653 --> 00:02:49,330
An OSNet re-identification model, through Torchreid,

58
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:52,901
compares these features against people seen by other cameras.

59
00:02:54,393 --> 00:02:56,679
When enough walking frames are available,

60
00:02:56,816 --> 00:02:59,734
OpenGait adds gait and silhouette features.

61
00:02:59,909 --> 00:03:05,198
Appearance, gait, camera location, timestamp and expected transition time

62
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:08,354
are fused into a single global person ID,

63
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:11,215
with a camera trail and last known location.

64
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:12,968
No face is required.

65
00:03:14,463 --> 00:03:16,466
Every detection becomes an event.

66
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:19,340
The decision engine scores it by event type,

67
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,445
confidence, persistence and camera location,

68
00:03:22,504 --> 00:03:24,391
so a weapon, a fire,

69
00:03:24,566 --> 00:03:27,188
or the reappearance of a marked person rises above

70
00:03:27,208 --> 00:03:28,463
routine activity.

71
00:03:29,956 --> 00:03:32,926
The highest priority feed is switched automatically to the

72
00:03:32,946 --> 00:03:35,670
primary view of a custom web dashboard,

73
00:03:35,794 --> 00:03:39,524
alongside the multi-camera grid, live notifications,

74
00:03:39,544 --> 00:03:41,997
the person trail, and system status.

75
00:03:43,496 --> 00:03:47,213
Browser alerts and optional warning sounds notify the operator

76
00:03:47,233 --> 00:03:47,998
instantly.

77
00:03:48,187 --> 00:03:51,285
Snapshots and short evidence clips are saved,

78
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:53,798
and every incident is logged with its ID,

79
00:03:53,921 --> 00:03:57,329
time, camera, event type, confidence,

80
00:03:57,349 --> 00:04:00,859
priority, global person ID, evidence link,

81
00:04:00,893 --> 00:04:02,200
and review status.

82
00:04:03,706 --> 00:04:07,242
Together, this forms a six-layer real-time architecture:

83
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:11,572
video input, stream ingestion, the AI processing engine,

84
00:04:11,605 --> 00:04:13,479
the decision and event engine,

85
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:17,668
a FastAPI backend with MongoDB or PostgreSQL,

86
00:04:17,830 --> 00:04:20,039
and a React and Tailwind dashboard.

87
00:04:21,523 --> 00:04:25,163
Every frame from every camera follows one monitoring loop:

88
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:29,312
read, preprocess, detect, track, match,

89
00:04:29,332 --> 00:04:33,358
score, switch, notify, save, and log.

90
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:36,013
Operators can then review each incident,

91
00:04:36,072 --> 00:04:38,075
and confirm it or mark it as a false

92
00:04:38,095 --> 00:04:38,757
alarm.

93
00:04:40,256 --> 00:04:43,290
The system will be evaluated for detection accuracy,

94
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:47,246
false alarms, tracking continuity, cross-camera matching,

95
00:04:47,369 --> 00:04:50,634
ID switches, processing speed, latency,

96
00:04:50,668 --> 00:04:54,617
dashboard response, camera switching, and logging correctness.

97
00:04:56,113 --> 00:04:59,817
Compared with conventional CCTV, the difference is clear.

98
00:04:59,992 --> 00:05:02,961
Manual observation becomes AI monitoring.

99
00:05:03,149 --> 00:05:05,783
Passive display becomes active detection.

100
00:05:05,958 --> 00:05:09,043
Single-camera tracking becomes cross-camera identity.

101
00:05:09,219 --> 00:05:12,059
And manual evidence search becomes automatic,

102
00:05:12,105 --> 00:05:13,940
organised incident records.

103
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:19,756
VigiLense can serve universities, airports and transport hubs,

104
00:05:19,776 --> 00:05:23,441
shopping malls, hospitals, offices, banks,

105
00:05:23,461 --> 00:05:28,235
warehouses, and high-security facilities, with research value in detection,

106
00:05:28,307 --> 00:05:32,269
multi-object tracking, re-identification and gait recognition.

107
00:05:33,743 --> 00:05:35,321
It is built with Python,

108
00:05:35,341 --> 00:05:42,640
PyTorch, YOLO26, OpenCV, ByteTrack, Torchreid and OpenGait for intelligence;

109
00:05:42,699 --> 00:05:47,228
FastAPI, React, Tailwind and a database for the application;

110
00:05:47,377 --> 00:05:50,257
running on an RTX-class GPU with at least three

111
00:05:50,277 --> 00:05:51,120
cameras.

112
00:05:52,613 --> 00:05:55,093
The work is planned across eight months,

113
00:05:55,113 --> 00:05:57,244
from requirements and data collection,

114
00:05:57,278 --> 00:06:01,369
through training, tracking, re-identification and the dashboard,

115
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:04,873
to integration, testing and the final demonstration,

116
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:08,353
within an estimated budget of one hundred thousand rupees.

117
00:06:09,843 --> 00:06:13,741
Looking ahead, VigiLense can grow with ethically approved facial

118
00:06:13,761 --> 00:06:17,761
recognition, licence plate recognition, a mobile alert app,

119
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,125
edge and cloud deployment, role-based access,

120
00:06:21,145 --> 00:06:25,428
encrypted evidence, and integration with emergency response systems.

121
00:06:26,913 --> 00:06:30,501
VigiLense is a Computer Engineering final year project by

122
00:06:30,521 --> 00:06:34,135
Hassnain Khan, Khurram Ali Khan and Yasir Hassan,

123
00:06:34,271 --> 00:06:37,563
under the supervision of Doctor Syed Khawar Hussain Shah.

124
00:06:39,063 --> 00:06:40,073
VigiLense.

125
00:06:40,249 --> 00:06:43,011
Watching every feed, so nothing is missed.

126
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:43,797
Thank you.
